  end:['Talk to us about residential window tinting Christchurch-wide. Send a photo of the room, tell us what you want to improve and ask us to explain the next step.','Planning house window tinting Christchurch-wide? We can look at one troublesome window or several rooms together, keeping the light, privacy and appearance of your home in mind.'],
  problems:[
   ['A lounge that gets too hot','Use your favourite seat again. Heat-control film can reduce solar heat through suitable glass, helping make sunny living areas more comfortable without covering the window all day.'],
   ['Screens lost in bright light','Watch television or work at your desk with less distracting brightness. Anti-glare film can soften the light while keeping a level of daylight that suits the room.'],
   ['Carpets and furnishings fading','Sunlight can fade carpets, timber flooring, curtains, sofas and artwork. Fade-reduction film can reduce UV exposure and manage light or heat, depending on the product. It cannot stop every cause of fading.'],
   ['Neighbours looking into your home','Enjoy more daytime privacy without keeping the curtains closed. Reflective film depends on the light balance; frosting is an option where privacy matters more than a clear view.'],
   ['Bathrooms and entrances on show','Obscure the view through bathroom windows, front-door glass and sidelights. Frosted film admits soft light; opaque products vary, so compare a sample before deciding.'],
   ['Glass you are worried about','Ask about film that can help hold broken glass together when the glass and installation are suitable. Safety film has a different job from privacy or surface-protection film.']
  ],
  choices:[
   ['Fade reduction window films','Help care for furniture, flooring and artwork exposed to sunlight. We compare UV, light and heat performance alongside the appearance you want to keep.'],
   ['Privacy window films','Reduce daytime overlooking in living rooms and bedrooms. We explain when reflective film works and what to use if you need privacy with the lights on at night.'],
   ['Heat control window films','Reduce solar heat entering sunny rooms. Choose around the glass and exposure, rather than assuming the darkest film will give the best result.'],
   ['Anti-glare window films','Make bright rooms more comfortable for screens, reading and relaxing. Compare suitable samples from your usual seat, not just beside the window.'],
   ['Frosted and opaque window films','Create privacy on bathrooms, entrances and internal glass. Plan full or partial coverage around where people can see in and how much light you want.'],
   ['Safety and security window films','Discuss help holding broken glass together and any specific protection needs. The product, glass, frame and installation must suit the intended purpose.']
  ],
  faqs:[
   ['Do I need every window tinted?','No. Start with the rooms that need attention. Different rooms may need different films, and some windows may not need treatment. We can help you compare a targeted approach with a larger installation.'],
   ['Can I keep the view and natural light?','Many transparent films preserve a view out, with different levels of colour and reflection. Frosted and opaque products obscure the outlook. Compare a suitable sample inside and outside before making your choice.'],
   ['Does privacy film work at night?','Reflective film is a daytime option when outside is brighter than inside. It does not give reliable privacy with lights on inside after dark. Frosted film obscures the view in both conditions; its coverage still needs planning.'],
   ['Can film go on double glazing?','The film must suit the glass, including its coatings and exposure. We check the application before recommending a product. Do not choose a film on colour or price alone.'],
   ['Can you help me choose a film for my house?','Yes. For house window tinting Christchurch-wide, share the room, approximate pane sizes and your main concern. We can discuss samples, suitability, installation and care without expecting you to choose a product first.']
  ]
