  intro:['A scratched shopfront can leave an otherwise well-kept business looking neglected. We fit anti graffiti window films Christchurch-wide to add a replaceable protective layer to suitable exposed glass.','If the film is damaged, it may be possible to replace that layer rather than the pane underneath. We assess the surface and the risk before recommending a product. Existing scratches or etching in the glass are not repaired by covering them with film.'],
  end:['For anti graffiti window films Christchurch-wide, send a photo of the exposed glass and any existing damage. We can discuss suitability, maintenance, replacement and fitting arrangements around your premises.'],
  problems:[['Scratches on customer-facing glass','Repeated marking can spoil a shopfront’s appearance. A suitable protective film offers a replaceable surface, helping care for the underlying glass.'],['Etching that leaves permanent damage','Etching can affect bare glass and lead to costly replacement. Discuss the type of exposure and a film suitable for the surface; no layer should be presented as protection against every attack.'],['Large panes costly to replace','Replacing a damaged film layer may be a more practical option than replacing intact underlying glass. Actual cost depends on the pane, access and extent of the damage.'],['Busy entrances and public paths','Street-facing windows and doors can be exposed to regular contact. We consider where damage is occurring and which surface needs protection.'],['A frontage you want to keep clear','A clear-looking protective layer can help maintain presentation without an intentionally dark finish. Check the selected product’s appearance and suitability.'],['Maintenance after damage','Plan what happens if the layer is marked again. Inspection and appropriate replacement help keep the protection useful rather than leaving a damaged surface in place.']],
  choices:[['A replaceable protective surface','The film takes surface wear or damage that might otherwise reach the glass. Its intended exposure, fitting surface and replacement arrangements need to suit the site.'],['Assessment before fitting','We look at the surface condition and existing damage. Film is not a repair for scratches already in the pane, and not every surface is a suitable application.'],['Care and replacement','Keep the product and cleaning guidance. If the film is scratched or etched, ask about assessment and replacement before attempting repairs or aggressive cleaning.'],['Commercial safety and security window films','For impact, broken fragments or forced-entry concerns, discuss a separate protection requirement. Anti-graffiti film is selected for surface protection, not proof of security performance.'],['Frosted and decorative window films','If privacy or branding matters too, explain the full requirement. Decorative appearance and surface protection are different jobs and need appropriate product selection.']],
  faqs:[['Will film repair scratches already in the glass?','No. Existing scratches and etching remain in the underlying glass. We discuss the condition before fitting and whether protection is appropriate for the surface as it stands.'],['What happens if the film is damaged?','The layer may be removed and replaced if the underlying glass remains suitable. We fit anti graffiti window films Christchurch-wide with replacement and maintenance needs considered from the start.'],['Is anti-graffiti film the same as safety film?','No. Anti-graffiti film protects the surface. Safety film is selected to help hold fragments together when a suitable pane breaks. Security claims need evidence for the complete proposed system.'],['Can film prevent every type of vandalism?','No. Suitability and protection depend on the product, application and incident. The film is a replaceable layer, not a guarantee that the pane cannot be damaged.'],['Can installation fit around our business?','Tell us your opening hours, access restrictions and which areas need to remain available. We discuss a practical installation plan before confirming the work.']]
