  end:['For commercial frosted and opaque window film Christchurch-wide, send photographs of the full glass layout and explain where privacy matters.','Ask about decorative window film Christchurch-wide if you want patterns, selected coverage or a branded detail. We can discuss suitable finishes, artwork requirements and fitting.'],
  problems:[['Meetings visible from the corridor','Obscure the areas people can see through while keeping the workplace open to daylight. Coverage should consider both seated and standing views.'],['Reception glass without a clear finish','Give the arrival area a consistent appearance. Align the treatment with the frames, adjoining panes and the way people move through the space.'],['Staff areas needing visual privacy','Create a clearer division between public and staff areas. Frosting changes the view through the glass; it does not make a room soundproof.'],['Offices beside work areas','Screen selected views without creating a solid wall. The finish and light transmission need to suit both sides of the glass.'],['Clear glass that feels too exposed','A full pane is not always necessary. Selected bands or sections may give the coverage you need while leaving useful clear areas.'],['Branding that should belong in the room','Patterns or logo-style details can make glass part of your interior. Agree the artwork, scale and alignment before the film is cut and fitted.']],
  choices:[['Frosted window film','Admit diffuse light while obscuring clear views. Choose the finish and coverage around how closely people approach the glass and the privacy required.'],['Opaque window film','Consider stronger visual screening where the outlook is not needed. Products vary in light transmission, so compare the selected sample rather than assuming it is blackout.'],['Decorative window film','We supply decorative window film Christchurch-wide for suitable patterns, bands and logo-style treatments. The agreed layout should make the design and coverage clear before fitting.'],['Full or partial coverage','Review the whole partition or frontage, including doors and adjoining panes. Consistent heights and edges help the finished treatment look like part of the building.'],['Commercial anti-glare window films','If the problem is harsh sunlight rather than overlooking, explore transparent light control separately. Privacy frosting is not a direct substitute for every solar or glare-control application.']],
  faqs:[['Does frosted film provide sound privacy?','No. Frosting obscures views; it does not soundproof a meeting room. If spoken privacy matters, that needs a separate assessment of the room and its construction.'],['Can the finish include our logo?','Suitable decorative treatments can be discussed around your artwork and glass. We confirm the proposed layout and requirements before fitting rather than assuming every design will suit every surface.'],['Will it block all daylight?','Frosting admits diffuse light. Opaque and blackout products have different light transmission, so check the actual product. The area covered also changes how the room feels.'],['Can some of the glass stay clear?','Yes, full and partial coverage can be discussed. Consider seated and standing views, adjoining panes and the appearance from both sides when agreeing the layout.'],['Can you fit around office hours?','We discuss access, room availability and the person who can approve the work. Timing and disruption are agreed for the building before installation.']]
